{
  "name": "ERP Purchase Order & Inventory Sync Automator",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 📦 ERP PURCHASE ORDER & INVENTORY SYNC AUTOMATOR\n**What it does:** Pulls new/updated purchase orders from your ERP REST API every morning → dedupes by PO number → logs them to Google Sheets → AI reviews each PO for anomalies → big or flagged POs wait for your Telegram approval (decision written back to the ERP) → approved POs sync inventory quantities → low-stock items trigger a reorder alert → one Telegram run summary.\n\n**You'll need:**\n- An ERP with a REST API that exposes purchase orders (Odoo, ERPNext, or a custom ERP)\n- OpenAI API key (platform.openai.com)\n- Google Sheets OAuth2 credentials\n- Telegram bot token + your chat ID (@BotFather → /newbot)\n\n**Status flow in Sheets:** `NEW` → `PENDING_APPROVAL` → `APPROVED` / `REJECTED` → `SYNCED` (auto-approved POs skip straight to `APPROVED`)",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 7460,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "f68e4ad6-e9d5-4f1b-a53b-793621d6916d",
      "name": "STICKY — Title",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -240,
        -160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 1 — Pull purchase orders from the ERP API\nDaily schedule trigger → HTTP GET on your ERP purchase-orders endpoint (paginated: page + per_page) → normalize into PO number / supplier / total / currency / lines.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 1160,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "87168968-d2fd-4af7-9b3a-b99cb717d264",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -240,
        180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 2 — Dedupe + log to Google Sheets\nRead PO numbers already in the sheet → keep only new POs → append rows with status `NEW`. Re-runs never double-process a PO.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 980,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "e5e79fe6-f485-411b-8599-cddf3e6395a9",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        940,
        180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 3 — AI anomaly review\nAI Agent reviews each PO with a Structured Output Parser (risk flag, risk level, one-line summary) → sheet gets the AI verdict.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 700,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "4944ad5a-af56-4b4a-b102-940fda9a0e63",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1900,
        180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 4 — Approval routing\nPO total ≥ threshold OR AI flagged → status `PENDING_APPROVAL` → Telegram 'Send and Wait' approval message → Approve writes the decision back to the ERP API and flips the sheet to `APPROVED`; Reject flips it to `REJECTED` and stops that PO cleanly. Low-risk POs auto-approve.",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 1460,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "d65bf41e-e9c3-4520-918d-09a990c137c3",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2620,
        20
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 5 — Inventory sync + low-stock alerts\nApproved POs: split into line items → update the Inventory sheet (Quantity On Order per SKU) → PO flips to `SYNCED` → read inventory levels → any SKU below its reorder level triggers a Telegram low-stock alert.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 2180,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "123f038f-e95f-454f-8b71-d2863345d355",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        4060,
        180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 6 — Run summary notification\nBoth sync branches merge → one Telegram summary: POs pulled, new POs, AI-flagged, low-stock items.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 1000,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "ac042f1b-dd00-4a3f-ac9b-05e9ec69a41d",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 6",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        6220,
        180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "hours",
              "hoursInterval": 24,
              "triggerAtHour": 9,
              "triggerAtMinute": 0
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "0f5594d5-e271-41cf-91f0-a20e8a99ef8e",
      "name": "Daily 9AM Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "4d7adb22-6160-41b1-8e9f-254d38a8d90f",
              "name": "erp_api_base_url",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "PASTE_YOUR_ERP_API_BASE_URL"
            },
            {
              "id": "18135969-6080-46d2-a522-d20df61298d1",
              "name": "erp_api_key",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "PASTE_YOUR_ERP_API_KEY"
            },
            {
              "id": "eda2400d-6f21-48d2-b5fa-723109e2f241",
              "name": "po_endpoint",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "/api/v1/purchase-orders"
            },
            {
              "id": "504ed381-08e2-45b1-a8f3-78e5b291b331",
              "name": "page_size",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "50"
